{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1558635716,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0NDc4MDczNDg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3455","origin":"github"},"title":"Unification of behavior and API of `create_sibling*`","message":"Originally posted to https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/3447\n\n`create_sibling_gitlab` essentially runs without any arguments and still does its job, given that it can find (or is pointed to) the required configuration in a superdataset that represent the origin or seed point of a dataset collection/hierarchy. This could be a model that could be applied to other `create_sibling*` commands too. If we do that, we finally have a straightforward path to replacing `create_sibling()` with an actual wrapper command that can call the appropriate actual implementation for a given target (thx to @bpoldrack for pointing this out). We could then (finally) revert the rename of `create_sibling_sshwebserver`. The common API would then be:\n\n```\ncreate-sibling-... -d \u003cdswithconfig\u003e -s NAME -r -R \u003cint\u003e --publish-depend \u003clabel\u003e [PATH [PATH ...]]\n```\n\nwhere `PATH` is a directory with (a) specific dataset(s) to create a sibling for. Any other option not listed above is considered implementation specific, and a command must come with the ability to read its value from a configuration, if not given.","files":null}]}